                <pb facs="0603" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13394: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-11T09:00:00+08:00">March 11, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 10—11:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. Following from American Consul General at Hankow.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“March 10, 6 p.m. My March 7, 1 p.m. Situation in vicinity Hwangshihkong has
                        cleared and <hi rendition="#italic">Tutuila</hi> returned Hankow today.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
